  "notes": "{任|まか}せる is a transitive ichidan verb meaning to entrust something to someone or let something take its course.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pattern: [person]⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{任|まか}せる\n\nTWO MAIN MEANINGS:\n1. To entrust to a person: ⟦{仕事|しごと}→仕事：00480_shigoto⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{任|まか}せる (entrust work)\n2. To leave to fate/nature: ⟦{流|なが}れ→流れ：03504_nagare⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{任|まか}せる (go with the flow)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦お{任|まか}せ→おまかせ：08310_omakase⟧⟦します→する：00392_suru⟧: I'll leave it to you (polite, often at restaurants)\n- {任|まか}せて!: Leave it to me!\n- ⟦{運|うん}→運：02143_un⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{天|てん}→天：noentry⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{任|まか}せる: to leave it to fate\n- ⟦{成|な}り{行|ゆ}き→成り行き：07311_nariyuki⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{任|まか}せる: to let things take their course\n- ⟦{自然|しぜん}→自然：01423_shizen⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{任|まか}せる: to let nature take its course\n\nRESTAURANT USAGE:\n⟦お{任|まか}せ→おまかせ：08310_omakase⟧ means \"chef's choice\" - the chef decides what to serve.",
